  "body": "## What's new in v2.4.1\n\n**Brand names are written exactly as you choose them.** If you type a brand under **Other**, that exact spelling now goes onto the tag and into Spoolman. Previously the app quietly swapped in its own capitalisation when it recognised the name, so a typed \"Jayo\" was written as \"JAYO\" while the form still showed \"Jayo\". The Brand list also shows the spelling from your own Spoolman server rather than the built-in one, so a vendor you created as \"Tecbears\" is now pickable instead of being hidden behind \"TECBEARS\".\n\nFilaments you already saved keep their current names. Only new ones use the corrected spelling, because renaming a vendor row would rewrite every filament pointing at it.\n\n**A Clear button in the top left.** One tap empties the form. It greys out when there is nothing to clear, so the button never does nothing. This replaces the **Clear all** row that v2.4 put in the `\u22ee` menu.\n\n**The `\u22ee` icon opens Settings directly.** With Clear all moved to its own button, the menu held a single row, so the popup was a tap in the way of the only thing behind it.\n\n**Writing a tag without Spoolman shows the prompt again.** With no Spoolman URL configured, tapping Write armed the tag reader but showed no \"Tap a tag to write\" message and no animation, so it looked like nothing had happened.\n\n### Notes\n\n- Reported on issue #8: the brand-casing bug. Thanks for the screenshot, it proved both preconditions.\n- 643 unit tests, 0 failures.\n- Same package (`com.spoolpainter.app`), in-place update, nothing to migrate.\n\n### Known issue\n\nBlank NTAG tags that have never been NDEF-formatted are misclassified as vendor tags and refused, with the write never attempted. This is the cause of the recurring \"NFC is hit and miss\" reports and is **not** fixed in this release. Root cause is proven and it is next up. Workaround: format the tag once with NFC Tools and it stays formatted.\n\n### Downloads\n\n`app-release.apk` for sideloading, `app-release.aab` for Play.\n"
